DESCRIPTION >
    Wave-3 flexible_report Class-A dim-swap: group_by=STITCHING_METHOD. Clone of
    flexible_report_attribution_status_by_site with the dim expr swapped to
    GROUP_COLUMNS.stitching_method (STITCHING_METHOD_SQL, attribution-engine.js:83) and the SAME
    external_event_id dedup carried from birth (#170). One row per stitching_method with the metric.

    INDEPENDENT DIM (verified, NOT an alias of attribution_status): STITCHING_METHOD_SQL is its own SQL
    over its own column with its own fallback — COALESCE(NULLIF(stitching_method,''), multiIf(
    ingestion_method='server_routed','browser','unknown')) — vs attribution_status's 'attributed'/
    'unattributed'/'unknown'. MODEL-INDEPENDENT: GROUP_COLUMNS.stitching_method = STITCHING_METHOD_SQL
    for all 4 touch models, references only conversion props (stitching_method, ingestion_method), NO _nd
    touchpoint columns. So the window is a no-op (same reasoning as provider/attribution_status, proven
    GREEN on --live) and this ONE pipe serves group_by=stitching_method for all 4 touch models.

    dim = STITCHING_METHOD_SQL, typed-translated (§2.6): properties.stitching_method -> stitching_method
    (LowCardinality(Nullable(String)), events.datasource:34); properties.ingestion_method ->
    ingestion_method (LowCardinality(String), :32). EMPTY/NULL convention replicated EXACTLY (its own,
    not attribution_status's): COALESCE(NULLIF(stitching_method,''), multiIf(ingestion_method=
    'server_routed','browser','unknown')) — an empty/absent stitching_method falls through to the same
    fallback the HogQL uses, so buckets match. metric in {revenue, conversions} via the `metric` param.
    BASE-CASE GATE ONLY (no dim2/custom/filters, UTC, conversion_date); window-tolerant. Same params/
    output columns (dim_value, metric_value) so the wiring's positional remap stays byte-identical.

    external_event_id DEDUP (identical to the sibling pipes, #170): keep all null/empty-keyed rows; for a
    non-null key keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered, matching
    HogQL). Tie-break Tinybird event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket for a genuine duplicate (it
    shares stitching_method+value). PARAM SHAPE: {{ String(site_id) }} referenced TWICE (outer + dedup
    subquery); date params once. MANDATORY before deploy: `tb --cloud deploy --check` (ST_Staging, NOT
    prod). VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN.

NODE flexible_report_stitching_method_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        COALESCE(NULLIF(stitching_method, ''), multiIf(ingestion_method = 'server_routed', 'browser', 'unknown')) AS dim_value,
        {% if String(metric, 'conversions') == 'revenue' %}
        SUM(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)))
        {% else %}
        countIf(lower(coalesce(conversion_type, '')) != 'refund')
        {% end %} AS metric_value
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
      -- external_event_id dedup — carried from the sibling pipes (#170), faithful port of the HogQL
      -- leg (attribution-engine.js:2397-2409). KEEP every null/empty-keyed row; for a non-null key
      -- keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered). Tie-break Tinybird
      -- event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket for a genuine duplicate.
      AND (
        external_event_id IS NULL
        OR external_event_id = ''
        OR event_id IN (
          SELECT argMin(event_id, timestamp)
          FROM events
          WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
            AND event_type = '$conversion'
            AND external_event_id IS NOT NULL
            AND external_event_id != ''
          GROUP BY external_event_id
        )
      )
    GROUP BY dim_value
    ORDER BY metric_value DESC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
